irst time we experience that).\r\n\r\nScenario:\r\n1. Create a time series index with default mapping only\r\n2. Update mapping with\r\n```\r\n{\"@timestamp\": {\"type\": \"date\"}}\r\n```\r\nFor this mapping update `isDataStream` is `false` even though it was `true` previously.\r\n\r\nOne option to fix this is to pass existing mapping into `MappingParser#parse` and initialize `isDataStream` to a value based on it. I didn\u0027t want to mix this change in here.","Thanks for this explanation. Let\u0027s make fixing `MapperBuilderContext#isDataStream()` a followup of this change. As part of that change the ` \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()` part of the condition can be removed."],"path":"server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/index/mapper/DateFieldMapper.java","id":36737,"created_at":"2024-07-08T21:33:57Z","original_position":55,"side":"RIGHT","position":47,"submitted_on_commit":"f51dd2cd5350241e08accfe888e0c06d72861868","diff_hunk":"@@ -942,6 +947,30 @@ protected void parseCreateField(DocumentParserContext context) throws IOExceptio\n     }\n \n     private void indexValue(DocumentParserContext context, long timestamp) {\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper and TsidExtractingFieldMapper need to use timestamp value,\n+        // so when this is true we store it in a well-known place\n+        // instead of forcing them to iterate over all fields.\n+        //\n+        // DataStreamTimestampFieldMapper is present and enabled both\n+        // in data streams and standalone indices in time_series mode\n+        if (isDataStreamTimestampField \u0026\u0026 context.mappingLookup().isDataStreamTimestampFieldEnabled()) {","submitted_line":956},"generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The transition from iterating over `context.rootDoc().getFields()` to using `context.doc().getByKey(...)` significantly improves the efficiency of `postParse`. By having `DateFieldMapper` proactively flag multiple values and store the timestamp value